        "teacherMoves": "Begin with: 'Last lesson we noticed something strange in our farmer story — she gave the seeds water and warmth but some still did not grow. You wrote questions about this on our DQB. Today we are going to investigate that specific mystery.' Display the prompt on the board. After students write, use cold-calling with a warm tone: 'Akinyi, what did you predict? Let us hear your thinking.' After each response, say: 'Interesting. Does anyone have a different idea?' WAIT 8 SECONDS before moving on. Do not say correct or incorrect. Write all predictions on the board. Close the predict phase by saying: 'We now have competing ideas. Scientists call this having multiple hypotheses. Our job today is to find evidence that either supports or challenges what we have written here.'",
